  <title>On-screen braille display</title>
  <p>
    The on-screen braille display is a window intended for developers that shows what would be
    presented on a braille display.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-on-screen-braille-display">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>On-Screen Display</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Cell count</gui>: Sets the number of
          braille cells shown in the on-screen braille display. Default: 32. Range: 1 to 80.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Show braille dot patterns</gui>: Controls whether
          the on-screen braille display shows Unicode braille dot patterns instead of text
          characters. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Text color</gui>: Selects the text color
          for the on-screen braille display. Default: #000000.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Background color</gui>: Selects the
          background color for the on-screen braille display. Default: #ffffff.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-on-screen-display">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Braille</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle the on-screen braille display on and off</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
